# Drafted by Gemini (R25 endings), edited.

~ start
Narrator: Down in the cold shadow of the barrow, you listened to the ancient whisper behind the bark and chose to unfasten the lock.
Narrator: The goat skull cracks open in dark fire, and the Horned King rises from the mire with a crown of twisted blackthorn upon his brow.
Narrator: You kneel first in the wet bracken as the Crooked Tree splits wide, letting the old fey queen step forth into the night air.
Narrator: Across the valley, the timber houses of Wickermoor groan as fresh, hungry briars wind tight around every threshold and hearth.
Narrator: By the rusted rails, the Vagrant watches the dark bloom spread across the hills, his fiddle hanging silent at his side.
the_vagrant [sad]: You heard her weeping in the root and opened the door, though it breaks my heart to see what walks out.
Narrator: You rise again as the first instruments of her crooked rebirth, wearing her thorny grace like a heavy winter cloak.
Narrator: Above the silent village, the gargantuan moon smiles wider than before, and the endless night belongs entirely to the queen.
-> END
